<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE starlink-15-16 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 Starlink Group 15-16 (27 V2 Mini Optimized, SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
thrust SL/vac interpolated on ambient pressure, mdot from Isp, staging/fairing/coast events; vertical rise to 17.2 s (rule: config guidance),
pitch kick 4.670 deg over 10 s, gravity turn, linear-tangent upper-stage steering tan(theta)=0.5837-0.001364*(t-t_ign), solved by optimizer.
Vehicle config: SpaceX Falcon 9 Block 5 (reusable first stage, droneship recovery) (sim/vehicles/falcon9.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Falcon 9 Block 5 masses from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9 Block 5&#x27; spec table; thrust/Isp from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9&#x27; spec table (citing SpaceX); event times from SpaceX&#x27;s sl-15-16 timeline.
Throttle profile not published: stage 1 uses the average mdot implied by propellant/162 s burn time and cuts off at the published MECO; the unburned ~41 t stands in for landing propellant.
Not flown: LL2 NET 2026-10-27T04:45Z (Mon Oct 26 9:45 pm PDT), status Go; SFN agrees (B1082.26, OCISLY). File ends at SECO-1 (parking orbit); SES-2/deploy not simulated.
Published timeline (SpaceX): Max-Q 1:08, MECO 2:26, stage sep 2:30, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:56, SECO-1 8:39, SES-2 53:01, SECO-2 53:03, deploy 1:01:53.
Integration step 0.1 s (run via trajectory-deck/2026-10-24-batch/run_sim_fine.py) so the energy cutoff lands within a few m/s.
Sanity: SECO-1 T+527.2 s vs SpaceX T+8:39 (519 s); MECO 62.7 km, 2.01 km/s vs Iridium NEXT-7 webcast 64.0 km, 1.91 km/s (lighter payload).
Target (see launch config): insertion 162 km, apoapsis 266 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 155.44 deg; payload 15525 kg.
Pad: 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-10-27T04:45:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
